    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         Icon geometry set — 24 × 24 design grid, stroke-only outline style.

         Why geometry instead of an icon font: a font can be missing on a locked-down terminal, its
         glyph names change between versions, and it rasterises differently at 125/150 % DPI. These
         are pure vector paths: they scale to any DPI, recolour with a single Stroke binding and add
         no binary payload.

         Usage:
             <Path Data="{StaticResource Icon.Cart}"
                   Stroke="{DynamicResource Kacher.TextSecondary}" StrokeThickness="1.8"
                   StrokeLineJoin="Round" StrokeStartLineCap="Round" StrokeEndLineCap="Round" />

         or, for a key supplied by a view model:
             Data="{Binding IconKey, Converter={StaticResource IconKey}}"
         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

